  <model metaid="meta_icg_liver" id="icg_liver" name="model for icg elimination by the liver" substanceUnits="mmole" timeUnits="min" volumeUnits="litre" areaUnits="m2" lengthUnits="metre" extentUnits="mmole">
    <notes>
      <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <h1>Model for icg elimination by the liver</h1>
        <h2>Description</h2>
        <p>Model for hepatic elimination of indocyanine green
encoded in <a href="http://sbml.org">SBML</a> format.</p>
        <p>
          <strong>Assumptions:</strong>
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>indocyanine green is not metabolized; it is taken up by the liver
(OATP1B3) and excreted unchanged into bile (MRP2)</li>
          <li>a part of the indocyanine green in the liver returns into the sinusoidal
plasma (reflux), which is the slow secondary phase of the plasma curve</li>
          <li>bilirubin inhibits the uptake competitively</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The content of this model has been carefully created in a manual research effort.</p>
